# Stale bulletins (do not put last month on this week)

Harvest truth is `parishes/parish_status.json`. `ok` is a **lie** if the newsletter heading is older than the harvest Sunday.

## Do not

- Treat Google Drive, hashed Wix, Dropfiles, or `bulletin.pdf` as this week just because the file downloaded. Raphoe (`drive-1jmslbrliw`) stayed **19 July 2026** on the same Drive link and was still `ok`.
- Stamp the harvest Sunday on a parish page whose body is June/July/last Sunday. Live lie: title **23/08/2026**, body **Sunday 19 July 2026**.
- Revert H1 (`freshness_after_unknown_url` — read the PDF heading when the URL has no date) or H3 (last Sunday is stale; grace is ahead-only).
- Call a recipe fixed because a static URL still works.

## Do

- Read the heading date (PDF text or live OCR body). No heading date → say **unknown**, not `ok`.
- Keep an old file off the mega PDF (`is_stale`). `apply_freshness_safety_net` must also reject unknown-URL + old heading.
- Problems-tab stale stays stale until a **real** this-week file exists on the parish site.

Proved live 25/08/2026 still `ok` with old bodies: Raphoe 19/07, Banagher 28/06, Melmount 12/07, Ardstraw East 05/07.
